.TH FT891REMOTE-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "FT891Remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ft891remote\-server \- share a Yaesu FT\-891 over the network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ft891remote\-server
.RI [ --headless " [" --config " " FILE "] [" \-v ]]
.br
.B ft891remote\-server
.RB [ \-\-list\-audio | \-\-list\-ports | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs next to a Yaesu FT\-891 and serves its audio, PTT and CAT control to a
remote client. The radio is driven through its own CAT protocol, without
Hamlib: every setting the radio exposes over CAT, the whole MENU included, can
be read and changed from the client.
.PP
Audio travels over UDP, control over TCP. The PTT is sent on both at once, so a
lost datagram never leaves the radio transmitting, and the server releases it
by itself if the client goes silent. Transmission is refused outside the
amateur bands of the configured IARU region.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without a desktop session, logging to standard output. The settings are the
ones saved by the graphical interface: configure once with a display, then run
without one.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read an .ini file instead of the saved settings. Lets one machine serve several
radios, each with its own file and ports.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also log frequency and mode changes. Without it, only transmit switches,
connections and errors are logged.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-audio
Print every audio interface and device PortAudio can see, with the sample rate
each one accepts, then exit. Use the names it prints in an .ini file.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-ports
Print the serial ports, then exit. The FT\-891 shows two: CAT goes through the
Enhanced one (usually
.IR /dev/ttyUSB0 ),
the Standard one can carry RTS/DTR PTT.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/FT891Remote/FT891RemoteServer.conf
Settings: CAT port and speed, PTT method, audio devices, network ports,
password, IARU region.
.SH NOTES
Opening a serial port requires membership of the
.B dialout
group. The radio's menu 05\-06 CAT RATE must match the configured speed.
.PP
A systemd user unit is installed. Enable it with
.RB "\(aq" "systemctl --user enable --now ft891remote-server" "\(aq" ,
and allow it to run without an open session with
.RB "\(aq" "sudo loginctl enable-linger $USER" "\(aq" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ft891remote (1)
